  "fields": [
    {
      "entryId": "gal-3-29",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Belonging to Christ makes heirs of the promise. First principle: the seed promise funnels through the Seed — being in Him is being in Abraham's covenant; the land of the promise is the world to inherit.",
      "density": 2.5,
      "words": 36,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 28,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "gal-3-28",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "All one in Christ Jesus. First principle: the oneness is baptismal and covenantal — everyone who calls on the name of the Lord is one heir; the walls fell in the water.",
      "density": 2.3429,
      "words": 32,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 27,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "gal-6-16",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The rule of new creation carries peace and mercy to the true Israel. First principle: the Israel of God are the crested new-creation walkers — mercy sought for a people defined by the cross, not the flesh.",
      "density": 2.2964,
      "words": 37,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 24,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "gal-3-8",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "In thee shall all nations be blessed — the gospel four hundred years early. First principle: Scripture foresaw; Scripture preached — the justification of the heathen by faith was announced to the father of the faithful himself.",
      "density": 2.2393,
      "words": 37,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 23,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "gal-3-16",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The promise to Abraham culminates in one Seed — Christ. First principle: Paul argues from a singular noun; the promises made to Abraham's seed were made to the Person who is the Seed.",
      "density": 2.1393,
      "words": 33,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 23,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "gal-1-8",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The anathema guards the gospel from heaven's own messengers. First principle: the gospel is fixed once delivered — revelation's closed core outranks any later angelic revision, as Moses and John both warn.",
      "density": 2.1143,
      "words": 32,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 23,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "gal-3-10",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Law-keepers are under the law's curse for one lapse. First principle: the curse is total in demand and universal in reach — Deuteronomy's amen-line indicts every continuant who has ever stopped.",
      "density": 2.0321,
      "words": 31,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 22,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "gal-3-6",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Genesis 15:6 is the Galatian argument's foundation stone. First principle: righteousness by believing precedes law, circumcision, and works — the counting of faith as righteousness is the oldest gospel text.",
      "density": 2.0071,
      "words": 30,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 22,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": [
          "Genesis 15:6"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "gal-6-2",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Mutual bearing fulfills the law of Christ. First principle: the new law has a new verb — bear; the strong carrying the fallen is Christ's own load-bearing love continued.",
      "density": 1.9821,
      "words": 29,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 22,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "gal-3-17",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The confirmed covenant outranks the later law. First principle: chronology is theology — the promise is older, confirmed in Christ, and no later administration can cancel it.",
      "density": 1.9679,
      "words": 27,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 20,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "gal-4-4",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "When the fullness of time came, God sent forth His Son, made of a woman, made under the law. First principle: incarnation is timed, gendered, and legal — for redemption of those under law.",
      "density": 1.9357,
      "words": 34,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "gal-3-19",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Added because of transgressions, till the Seed should come, ordained by angels through a mediator. First principle: the law was a temporary tutor with a retirement date — the Seed's arrival ended its custodianship.",
      "density": 1.9357,
      "words": 34,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "gal-3-22",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The universal shut-up has one purpose: the promise given to believers. First principle: the conclusion is custody, not condemnation alone — all under sin so the faith-promise has no rival door.",
      "density": 1.9179,
      "words": 31,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 20,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "gal-3-11",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Habakkuk 2:4 is the verse that splits law from life. First principle: three apostles quote it — Romans doctrinally, Galatians polemically, Hebrews pastorally — life by faith, never by performance.",
      "density": 1.8929,
      "words": 30,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 20,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": [
          "Habakkuk 2:4"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "gal-4-30",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Sarah's demand becomes Scripture's verdict: the bondman shall not inherit. First principle: law-born and promise-born cannot co-inherit; the household of faith is fenced by the Word, not by sentiment.",
      "density": 1.8107,
      "words": 29,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "gal-4-5",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The fullness-of-time Son redeems law-dwellers into sonship. First principle: adoption is the purchase — redemption from under the law is the door to crying, Abba, Father.",
      "density": 1.7357,
      "words": 26,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "gal-3-13",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Christ has redeemed us from the curse of the law, being made a curse for us. First principle: the cross absorbs covenant curse so blessing can reach the nations.",
      "density": 1.6393,
      "words": 29,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 16,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "gal-4-27",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Isaiah 54 quoted for the freewoman's many children. First principle: the desolate Jerusalem-above has more children than the enslaved — grace's family outgrows the flesh's.",
      "density": 1.5964,
      "words": 25,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 17,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "gal-4-22",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "One by a bondmaid, one by a freewoman — the two-covenant allegory begins. First principle: the two sons map two covenants; the birth of each decides its household.",
      "density": 1.5571,
      "words": 28,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 15,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "gal-3-12",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Leviticus 18:5 states the law's own terms — doing, not believing. First principle: the law is not of faith by design; its engine is doing. Mixing the engines wrecks both.",
      "density": 1.55,
      "words": 30,
      "sentences": 3,
      "maxSentenceWords": 14,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
